        "timestamp": 1773399234
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks! I think having used <code>RingHom.ker</code> before, I only thought of searching for <code>Ideal</code>, not <code>TwoSidedIdeal</code>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th><strong>Ideal+IsTwoSided</strong></th>\n<th><strong>TwoSidedIdeal</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>RingHom</strong></td>\n<td><code>RingHom.ker</code></td>\n<td><code>TwoSidedIdeal.ker _.toNonUnitalRingHom</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>NonUnitalRingHom</strong></td>\n<td><code>(TwoSidedIdeal.ker _).asIdeal</code></td>\n<td><code>TwoSidedIdeal.ker</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>It seems weird that I have to use <code>TwoSidedIdeal</code> to fill in the bottom left and top right corners here, but the top left doesn't use <code>TwoSidedIdeal</code> at all. Is there a way to unify this?</p>",
        "id": 579353538,
        "sender_full_name": "Li Xuanji",
        "timestamp": 1773434717
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The plans I have (although I'm working on other things for the next few months) go as follows:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Make <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RingHom.ker#doc\">docs#RingHom.ker</a> accept only actual <code>RingHom</code>s (as opposed to a term of a <code>RingHomClass</code>).</li>\n<li>Define modules over non-unital rings. This will allow to generalize <code>Submodule</code> and <code>Ideal</code> to this new typeclass.</li>\n<li>Generalize material about <code>Ideal</code> to the setting of non-unital rings.</li>\n<li>Along with (3), define <code>NonUnitalRingHom.ker</code> as an <code>Ideal</code> (and of course it will be <code>IsTwoSided</code>).</li>\n</ol>",
        "id": 579354768,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1773435294
    }
]